# Reuse first

Before creating any class or widget:

1. Search `core/ui`, `core/engine`, `core/tools`, `data/models`, and `data/repositories` by name and by purpose.
2. If something similar exists, extend, compose, or parameterize it. Do not copy.
3. If a second feature needs a feature-private widget, move it to `core/ui/widgets/` instead of duplicating.

State in the response which existing classes were reused.

```dart
// BAD — second copy of a palette already in features/drawing/widgets
class HomeColorPalette extends StatelessWidget { ... }

// GOOD — the drawing palette moves to core/ui/widgets and both screens use it
class ColorPalette extends StatelessWidget { ... }
```
